But "not including v" for different v's are all valid (we just don't pick that v in the subset), so yes, for each s, new_dp[s] = min_{options} (dp[s] + op), because we pay op for the element regardless of inclusion.

Similarly, new_dp[s+v] = min over options with v ≤ sum-s of (dp[s] + op)

But careful: for a single element, we choose one option (v,op), then decide to include it or not in the subset. So for fixed s (subset sum from previous elements), when processing element with options, we:

- Choose an option (v,op), pay op
- Then either include v (if v ≤ sum-s) leading to s+v, or not include leading to s

